  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5f9a8925",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Shifted QR with Householder reduction and deflation converged for both graph Laplacians, requiring 675 iterations for clusters ($N = 400$) and 1035 iterations for moons ($N = 600$), using $\\texttt{tol}=10^{-8}$. \n",
    "\n",
    "The maximum eigenvalue errors were approximately $9.3\\cdot10^{-14}$ and $7.0\\cdot10^{-13}$, respectively, while the maximum eigenpair residuals were $9.6\\cdot10^{-9}$ and $4.6\\cdot10^{-8}$.\n",
    "\n",
    "Although the maximum off-diagonal element remains relatively large during much of the iteration process, the deflation plots show that the eigenvalues are continuously isolated. Deflation also makes later QR-steps cheaper by reducing the active matrix dimension."
   ]
  },
