   "source": [
    "All six experiments converged with small eigenpair residuals, of order $10^{-8}$.\n",
    "\n",
    "Increasing the matrix size from $N = 100$ to $N = 400$ increased the number of QR iterations from 194 to 658, while the runtime increased from 0.46s to 46.93s. This illustrates the high computational cost of dense QR iteration for larger matrices.\n",
    "\n",
    "For fixed $N = 200$, varying the graph density between 0.037 and 0.131 had relatively little effect on runtime or iteration count, with no clear trend in these experiments. This is consistent with the implementation converting sparse Laplacians to dense matrices and using general dense QR factorizations.\n",
    "\n",
    "Although Householder reduction produces a tridiagonal matrix, the current QR implementation does not fully exploit this structure. A structure-aware QR algorithm using Givens rotations could reduce the computational cost."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a186e32c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Lanczos Iteration"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "1a4e0d2e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "def lanczos_iteration(L, m, K=4, which=\"smallest\", v1=None, seed=0, reorth=False, tol=1e-12):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Compute the Ritz pairs of a symmetric matrix L using the Lanczos algorithm.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Parameters:\n",
    "        L: The graph Laplacian, symmetric (numpy array or scipy sparse matrix), shape (n, n)\n",
    "        m: The number of Lanczos steps\n",
    "        K: The number of Ritz pairs to return. If None, all m pairs are returned\n",
    "        which: \"smallest\" (for spectral clustering) or \"largest\"\n",
    "        v1: Initial vector. If None, a random vector is used\n",
    "        seed: The seed for the random number generator (used if v1 is None)\n",
    "        reorth: If True, w_j is re-orthogonalized against all previous v_i (not part of Alg. 6.15,\n",
    "                but prevents the loss of orthogonality / ghost eigenvalues in floating point)\n",
    "        tol: beta_{j+1} below tol * ||L v_j|| is treated as beta_{j+1} = 0 (breakdown).\n",
    "             If the algorithm stops early at step j, m is reduced to j.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Returns:\n",
    "        theta: Ritz values theta_i^(m), shape (K,)\n",
    "        U: Ritz vectors u_i^(m) = V_m y_i^(m) as columns, shape (n, K)\n",
    "        res: Residual norms |beta_m (e_m^T y_i^(m))|, shape (K,)\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "\n",
    "    n = L.shape[0]\n",
    "\n",
    "    # 1. Initial vector of 2-norm unity, beta_1 = 0, v_0 = 0\n",
    "    if v1 is None:\n",
    "        v1 = np.random.default_rng(seed).random(n)\n",
    "    V = np.zeros((n, m))\n",
    "    V[:, 0] = v1 / la.norm(v1)\n",
    "    alphas = np.zeros(m)\n",
    "    betas = np.zeros(m)\n",
    "    beta = 0.0\n",
    "    v_prev = np.zeros(n)\n",
    "\n",
    "    for j in range(m):\n",
    "        v = V[:, j]\n",
    "        w = L @ v - beta * v_prev                     # 3. w_j = L v_j - beta_j v_{j-1}\n",
    "        alpha = w @ v                                 # 4. alpha_j = (w_j, v_j)\n",
    "        w = w - alpha * v                             # 5. w_j = w_j - alpha_j v_j\n",
    "        if reorth:\n",
    "            w = w - V[:, :j + 1] @ (V[:, :j + 1].T @ w)\n",
    "        beta_next = la.norm(w)                        # 6. beta_{j+1} = ||w_j||_2\n",
    "\n",
    "        alphas[j] = alpha\n",
    "        betas[j] = beta_next\n",
    "\n",
    "        if beta_next <= tol * max(abs(alpha), beta, 1.0):   # 6. If beta_{j+1} = 0 then Stop\n",
    "            betas[j] = 0.0\n",
    "            m = j + 1\n",
    "            break\n",
    "        if j + 1 < m:\n",
    "            V[:, j + 1] = w / beta_next               # 7. v_{j+1} = w_j / beta_{j+1}\n",
    "        v_prev, beta = v, beta_next\n",
    "\n",
    "    V_m, alphas, betas = V[:, :m], alphas[:m], betas[:m]\n",
    "    T_m = np.diag(alphas) + np.diag(betas[:-1], 1) + np.diag(betas[:-1], -1)\n",
    "    beta_m = betas[-1]        # coefficient of v_{m+1} in L V_m = V_m T_m + beta_m v_{m+1} e_m^T\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Ritz values theta^(m) in sigma(T_m) and eigenvectors y^(m) of T_m (ascending order)\n",
    "    theta, Y = la.eigh(T_m)\n",
    "    K = m if K is None else min(K, m)\n",
    "    idx = np.arange(K) if which == \"smallest\" else np.arange(m - 1, m - K - 1, -1)\n",
    "    theta, Y = theta[idx], Y[:, idx]\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Ritz vectors u^(m) = V_m y^(m)\n",
    "    U = V_m @ Y\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Residual ||(L - theta^(m) I) u^(m)||_2 = |beta_m (e_m^T y^(m))|, where e_m^T y^(m) = Y[-1, :]\n",
    "    e_m = np.zeros(m)\n",
    "    e_m[-1] = 1.0\n",
    "    res = np.abs(beta_m * (e_m @ Y))\n",
    "\n",
    "    return theta, U, res\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "db19cc02",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We would now like to implement the Lanczos algorithm. The pseudocode we have used for this can be found in Saad Algorithm 6.16. It is given as:\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\begin{array}{rl}\n",
    "\\hline\n",
    "\\textbf{Algorithm 6.16} & \\textbf{Lanczos Method for Linear Systems} \\\\\n",
    "\\hline\n",
    "1. & \\text{Compute} \\quad r_0 = b - Ax_0, \\beta := ||r_0||_2, \\quad \\text{ and} \\quad v_1 := \\frac{r_0}{\\beta} \\\\\n",
    "2. & \\textbf{For } j = 1, 2, \\dots, m \\textbf{ Do} \\\\\n",
    "3. & \\quad w_j = A v_j - \\beta_j v_{j-1} \\quad(\\text{If}\\quad j = 1 \\quad \\text{set} \\quad \\beta_1v_0 \\equiv 0)\\\\\n",
    "4. & \\quad \\alpha_j = (w_j, v_j) \\\\\n",
    "5. & \\quad w_j := w_j - \\alpha_j v_j \\\\\n",
    "6. & \\quad \\beta_{j+1} = \\|w_j\\|_2. \\quad \\textbf{ If } \\quad \\beta_{j+1} = 0 \\quad \\textbf{then stop} \\\\\n",
    "7. & \\quad v_{j+1} = w_j / \\beta_{j+1} \\\\\n",
    "8. & \\textbf{end for} \\\\\n",
    "9. & \\text{Set} \\quad T_m = \\text{tridiag}(\\beta_i, \\alpha_i, \\beta_{i+1})\\quad \\text{and}\\quad V_m = [v_i, \\dots, v_m] \\\\\n",
    "10. & \\text{Compute} \\quad y_m = T_m^{-1}(\\beta e_1) \\quad \\text{and} \\quad x_m = x_0 + V_m y_m \\\\\n",
    "\\hline\n",
    "\\end{array}\n",
    "$$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "34469983",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Convergence of the Lanczos method\n",
    "\n",
    "We run `lanczos_iteration` on the blobs and moons Laplacians from `handin.ipynb` ($k = 10$, $\\sigma = 1$, seed 0) for $m = 1, \\dots, 200$ steps, with full reorthogonalization unless stated otherwise. Since the start vector is the same (seed 0), the run with $m$ steps continues the run with $m-1$ steps, so this gives the convergence history of the Ritz pairs. Reference: `lambdas`, `V` from `scipy.linalg.eigh`.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Theory (Lanczos.pdf).** The Ritz values converge to the extreme eigenvalues, $\\lambda_i - \\theta_i^{(m)} \\approx C e^{-2m\\mu_i}$, where $\\mu_i$ depends on the spectral gap. For the smallest eigenvalue the Chebyshev (Kaniel–Paige) bound gives\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\gamma_1 = \\frac{\\lambda_2 - \\lambda_1}{\\lambda_n - \\lambda_2}, \\qquad \\rho_1 = 1 + 2\\gamma_1 + 2\\sqrt{\\gamma_1^2 + \\gamma_1}, \\qquad \\mu_1 = \\log \\rho_1 ,\n",
    "$$\n",
    "so the eigenvector error and the residual decrease like $\\rho_1^{-m}$, and the eigenvalue error like $\\rho_1^{-2m} = e^{-2m\\mu_1}$. Here $\\lambda_2$ is the next *distinct* eigenvalue: started from one vector, Lanczos only sees one direction in each eigenspace."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "814a5c0b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Graph Laplacians as in handin.ipynb (gaussian and moons, k = 10, sigma = 1, seed 0)\n",
    "np.random.seed(0)\n",
    "X = make_data()\n",
    "C_gaussian, L_gaussian, lambdas_gaussian, V_gaussian = spectral_clustering(X, k=10, K=4, sigma=1)\n",
    "\n",
    "np.random.seed(0)\n",
    "Y = make_moons()\n",
    "C_moons, L_moons, lambdas_moons, V_moons = spectral_clustering(Y, k=10, K=4, sigma=1)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b243fffe",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def distinct(lambdas, tol0):\n",
    "    '''\n",
    "    Distinct eigenvalues of L (eigenvalues closer than tol0 are counted once).\n",
    "    Lanczos started from one vector only \"sees\" one direction per eigenspace, so these are\n",
    "    the eigenvalues the Ritz values converge to.\n",
    "    '''\n",
    "    d = [lambdas[0]]\n",
    "    for lam in lambdas[1:]:\n",
    "        if lam - d[-1] > tol0:\n",
    "            d.append(lam)\n",
    "    return np.array(d)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def lanczos_rate(lambdas, i, tol0):\n",
    "    '''\n",
    "    Theoretical convergence factor 1/rho_i of the i-th smallest Ritz pair (Chebyshev / Kaniel-Paige bound)\n",
    "    '''\n",
    "    d = distinct(lambdas, tol0)\n",
    "    gamma = (d[i + 1] - d[i]) / (lambdas[-1] - d[i + 1])\n",
    "    return 1 / (1 + 2 * gamma + 2 * np.sqrt(gamma**2 + gamma))\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def lanczos_history(L, M, reorth=True, Q=None):\n",
    "    '''\n",
    "    Run lanczos_iteration for m = 1, ..., M steps (same start vector, so step m continues step m-1)\n",
    "    and record the Ritz pairs after every step.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Parameters:\n",
    "        L: The graph Laplacian\n",
    "        M: The maximum number of Lanczos steps\n",
    "        reorth: Passed on to lanczos_iteration\n",
    "        Q: Optional orthonormal basis of a reference eigenspace; the distance of the smallest\n",
    "           Ritz vector to it, ||u - Q Q^T u||, is recorded as eigenvector error\n",
    "\n",
    "    Return:\n",
    "        dict with lists over m of: theta (all m Ritz values), res (their residuals),\n",
    "        orth (||U^T U - I|| of all m Ritz vectors) and vec_err (if Q is given)\n",
    "    '''\n",
    "    h = dict(ms=np.arange(1, M + 1), theta=[], res=[], orth=[], vec_err=[])\n",
    "    for m in h[\"ms\"]:\n",
    "        theta, U, res = lanczos_iteration(L, m, K=None, reorth=reorth)\n",
    "        h[\"theta\"].append(theta)\n",
    "        h[\"res\"].append(res)\n",
    "        h[\"orth\"].append(la.norm(U.T @ U - np.eye(U.shape[1])))\n",
    "        if Q is not None:\n",
    "            u = U[:, 0]\n",
    "            h[\"vec_err\"].append(la.norm(u - Q @ (Q.T @ u)))\n",
    "    return h\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def column(h, key, i):\n",
    "    '''Value number i (i-th smallest Ritz pair) of h[key] for every m, NaN while m <= i.'''\n",
    "    return np.array([x[i] if len(x) > i else np.nan for x in h[key]])\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "M = 200\n",
    "tol0_gaussian = 1e-10 * lambdas_gaussian[-1]\n",
    "tol0_moons = 1e-10 * lambdas_moons[-1]\n",
    "m0_gaussian = np.sum(lambdas_gaussian < tol0_gaussian)    # multiplicity of lambda = 0 (connected components)\n",
    "m0_moons = np.sum(lambdas_moons < tol0_moons)\n",
    "\n",
    "hist_gaussian = lanczos_history(L_gaussian, M, Q=V_gaussian[:, :m0_gaussian])\n",
    "hist_moons = lanczos_history(L_moons, M, Q=V_moons[:, :m0_moons])\n",
    "hist_gaussian_noreorth = lanczos_history(L_gaussian, M, reorth=False)"
   ]
  },
