    "**Loss of orthogonality.** Without reorthogonalization (plain Algorithm 6.15) the Ritz vectors lose their orthogonality exactly while the smallest Ritz pair converges (from $10^{-10}$ at $m = 31$ to order 1 at $m = 74$), until $\\|U^TU - I\\|_2$ is of order 1. This is Paige's result: in floating point, the Lanczos vectors lose orthogonality in the direction of converged Ritz vectors. With full reorthogonalization the error stays around $10^{-13}$. The residual of the smallest pair is the same in both runs until it has converged, so loss of orthogonality does not slow down convergence, but it produces duplicate Ritz values and Ritz vectors that are not orthogonal."
